0: //! Broadcast messages to and cache messages from untrusted peers.
1: //!
2: //! # Overview
3: //!
4: //! The core of the module is the [Engine]. It is responsible for:
5: //! - Accepting and caching messages from other participants
6: //! - Broadcasting messages to all peers
7: //! - Serving cached messages on-demand
8: //!
9: //! # Message Caching
10: //!
11: //! The engine receives messages from other peers and caches them. The cache is a bounded queue of
12: //! messages per peer. When the cache is full, the oldest message is removed to make room for the
13: //! new one.
14: //!
15: //! Messages referenced by multiple senders stay cached until the last per-sender deque that
16: //! contains them is evicted (meaning redundant messages are only stored once).
17: //!
18: //! # Peer Management
19: //!
20: //! Only peers in `latest.primary` may buffer messages (see [commonware_p2p::Provider]). When a peer
21: //! is no longer in `latest.primary`, its buffered messages are evicted unless buffered by any other
22: //! primary peer.
